{{also|Borer}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{suffix|en|bore|er|id2=agent noun}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈbɔːɹə/}}
* {{a|US}} {{enPR|bôrʹər}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈbɔːɹɚ/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɔːɹə(ɹ)|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A tool used for [[drilling]].
# A person who bores or drills; a person employed to drill bore holes.
# A [[tedious]] person; a person who bores others; a [[bore]].
# An [[insect]] or insect [[larva]] that bores into wood.
# One of the many types of [[mollusc]] that bore into soft rock.
# A [[cyclostome]], such as a [[hagfish]], which bore into [[injured]], dead, or [[decaying]] sea creatures to feed on their flesh.

{{Webster 1913}}

